==English==
[[Image:WSJ2007_TerraVille_Stilts.JPG|thumb|A girl on '''stilts''' (walking poles).]]
[[Image:Himantopus himantopus, Sète cf26.jpg|A '''stilt''' (bird)|thumb|right]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stilte}}, {{m|enm|stulte}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*stilte}}, {{m|ang|*stylte}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*stiltijǭ}}, {{m|gem-pro|*staltijǭ}}, {{m|gem-pro|*stultijǭ|t=stilt}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*stelt-|t=to be stiff}}. Akin to {{cog|da|stylte}}, {{cog|nl|stelt}}, {{cog|de|Stelze}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/stɪlt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪlt}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two [[pole]]s with footrests that allow someone to stand or walk above the ground; used mostly by [[entertainer]]s.
# A tall [[pillar]] or [[post]] used to support some [[structure]]; often above [[water]].
# Any of various [[wading bird]]s of the genera ''[[Himantopus]]'' and ''[[Cladorhynchus]]'', related to the [[avocet]], that have extremely long legs and long thin [[bill]]s.
# A [[crutch]].
# The [[handle]] of a [[plough]].
#: {{rfquotek|en|Halliwell}}

====Derived terms====
* {{vern|black-necked stilt}} (''{{ll|mul|Himantopus mexicanus}}'')
* {{vern|stilt plover}} ({{taxlink|Himantopus knudseni|species|ver=190416}})
* [[stilt sandpiper]] (''{{ll|mul|Calidris himantopus}}'')

